From 59c4b955542ea0f285c99fcc0c9da7b293c21fd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:56:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(app): refusals say what a setup owns in plain words,
 not "furniture"

Review round on #886: the "not a model" refusals fire for tools,
operations, setups and program entries too, so "part of a setup" was
false there. They now say "is not a model - it is a setup's stock or
work offset, a setup, a tool, an operation or other CAM data"; the
fixture tag refusal uses the same condition and sentence. New test
checks a tool and an operation through RepairModel and UpdateModel.

Fixes #878

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
